# One line-ending truth across both machines (Linux laptop / Windows
# partition): every text file is LF in the repository AND in the working
# tree. Editors and tools on both sides (VS Code, git-bash, PowerShell,
# python, node) read and write LF fine, and a mixed-EOL working tree is
# what happens otherwise — the Windows checkout previously rendered CRLF
# (Git-for-Windows' system core.autocrlf=true) while LF-preferring tools
# inserted their own lines into it, producing `w/mixed` files.
# Binaries are pinned explicitly so future formats never rely on
# auto-detection; eol=lf beats any local core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png -text
*.webp -text
*.jpg -text
*.wav -text
